			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tU_BUjd7nFGkJl7Yn",
			"name": "Bio-plasma",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A bio-cannon that spits a searing, self-sustaining ball of superheated bile — the Carnifex's answer to an Imperial plasma weapon, grown rather than engineered, and just as capable of punching through power armour. Codex: Tyranids background across editions singles out bio-plasma as one of the most dangerous ranged weapons a Carnifex can be grown to carry, a real threat to Terminator-grade plate rather than merely power armour.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this weapon by dice, only by role (\"a Carnifex spit\" capable of matching Imperial plasma per this project's brief); it is built directly on framework.md's own Plasma Gun anchor (6d×4(3) burn ex) rather than a re-derived figure, the same judgement this project's Necron Particle Beamer entry makes against the same anchor, since bio-plasma's fictional role — kills Marines through power armour, a real if inconsistent threat to Terminators — is identical to plasma's own. Innate Attack (Burn) (B61, 5/die) at an effective 24 dice (6 base x4 multiplier) = 120, with Explosion (+50%) and Armor Divisor (3) (+100%): net +150%, 120x2.5=300 — identical cost math to the Heavy Venom Cannon above, since both use the same 5-point-per-die type rate and the same modifier stack; only the damage type (burn vs. crush) differs. Checked by exact dice distribution (identical to the Heavy Venom Cannon's own figures, since the dice and divisor match): clears every personal-armour DR at 99.9%+, Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 66.7) at 85.5%, and the vehicle table at 0%-99.5% across AV10-14 — a genuine, reliable threat to power armour and a real (if not overwhelming) one to Terminator plate, exactly matching bio-plasma's fictional reputation. Handling: Acc 3 and 150/450 range, shorter than the Heavy Venom Cannon's own reach since a spat globule of bile doesn't fly as flat or as far as a solid mass; Shots 3(90), matching the Heavy Venom Cannon's own regrowth figures for a comparably huge single organ.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
